# a part of the day fused with TODAY, as English "tonight" is: "i" before a
# bare part-of-day noun names today's band.  "i kväll" is "this evening,
# tonight" and "i natt" is "tonight" or "last night"
# (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/i_kväll,
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/i_natt); "i förmiddag" and "i eftermiddag"
# follow the same pattern, as Norwegian "i ettermiddag tar jeg fri" does
# (Bokmålsordboka, ettermiddag, https://ordbokene.no/bm/13299).
i förmiddag
i formiddag
i eftermiddag
i kväll
i kvall
i natt
